     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg per day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg per day for immediate-release metformin, and 2,000 mg per day for extended-release in many labels. A single 1700 mg dose is also well above the typical maximum of 1,000 mg per dose. This dose would put the patient at serious risk of lactic acidosis.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg per day, the maximum.\n- **1000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg per day.\n- **1700 mg total per day.** This could be 850 mg twice daily, or about 566 mg three times daily, which isn't a standard strength.\n- Another dose you have in mind.\n\nIf you do want 1700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that you confirmed the dose. I'd still recommend a second check first. Once you confirm, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
     ],
